		<a name="50593"></a>
		<img src="icon_mi_1.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;03/31/2005&nbsp;:&nbsp; 10:53:54</font>

		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=241"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
			&nbsp;<a href="JavaScript:openWindow('pop_mail.asp?id=241')"><img src="icon_email.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Email Poster" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

				&nbsp;<a href="privatesend.asp?method=Topic&mname=H. Halgernon"><img src="pm.gif" width="11" height="17" alt="Send H. Halgernon a Private Message" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=50593&TOPIC_ID=8290&FORUM_ID=14&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=New+Adventures+%2D+General+Board&Topic_Title=E%27ci+is+going+away%2E&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I think EQ1 will be around for a loooong time still (ala UO), but I think we're seeing it's marginalization as a force in the MMORPG market.  What we're seeing the end of are the days when the success or failure of a new game is compared to EQ.</P><P>WoW has definitively taken EQ1's crown as the 800-pound gorilla of the industry.  Plus EQ2 was destined to be a big draw away from EQ1 for quite a few folks.  (Though I think it's a better way to go than EA's plan to let UO languish with no successor.)</P><P><BLOCKQUOTE id=quote><font size=1 face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" id=quote>quote:<hr height=1 noshade id=quote>It's funny, I logged on my free AO account (a game I REALLY expected to be gone by now) and it's still alive and kicking well. Quite a few newbies in the newbie zone (Kaashar's guage of how well a MMOG's doing; check the newbie zones. If you start seeing them empty the game is on it's way out).<hr height=1 noshade id=quote></BLOCKQUOTE id=quote></font id=quote><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size=2 id=quote></P><P>AO did something brilliant - you can download the core game (no expansions) and play it for FREE.  This gets newbies into the game who then only need to purchase the expansions they want and start paying a subscription fee if they get hooked and want more content.<img src=icon_smile_blush.gif border=0 align=middle>  I think much like the periodic free trials all MMOGs seem to give nowadays that this practice will become common.</P><P>Regardless of that though, EQ1 will be around for a good long while yet.  It just won't be huge.  There are still people who won't leave Meridian 59, so I have to imagine that there's people who will be trying to take their EQ phat lewtz to their graves. <img src=icon_smile_tongue.gif border=0 align=middle><img src=icon_smile_dead.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P>As for us, I think we should keep the "Arbiters of E'ci" in our logo.  I think we had a pretty good server culture going there, and I like the historical context. <img src=icon_smile_big.gif border=0 align=middle>  I still think we should have a re-worked picture with a WoW setting though, as WoW is the game that has revitalized us as a gaming group.</P><P>Good luck to you folks still playing EQ1!  I hope "Tunare" turns out to be as nice a homeworld as E'ci was.<img src=icon_smile.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P>- Hally Halgernon, Office Gnome.<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
